     set: each kept the placeholder point it shared with its neighbour, still
     byte-identical to its pre-2.1.0 value, so no OpenStreetMap value was ever
     written to either and no ODbL claim is made over them.

   A commune centre is one value repeated across representations, so the ODbL
   covers these 323 coordinates wherever they appear: data/algeria.json,
   data/communes_w1_w23.json, data/communes_w24_w48.json,
   data/communes_w49_w69.json, data/csv/communes.csv,
   data/geojson/communes.geojson and data/sql/full.sql.

   The other 1,218 commune coordinates are not OpenStreetMap-derived and no ODbL
   claim is made over them.

3. Wilaya capital points

   A wilaya's latitude / longitude is the centre of its capital commune
   (capital_commune_code), the same value and not a second reading of it, so it
   carries whatever terms that commune centre carries. 6 of the 69 wilaya capital
   points are therefore among the OpenStreetMap-derived coordinates above and are
   ODbL 1.0, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors: wilayas 7 (Biskra, commune 701),
   16 (Alger Centre, 1601), 25 (Constantine, 2501), 32 (El Bayadh, 3201),
   52 (Beni-Abbes, 5201) and 61 (El Kantara, 717). They appear in
   data/algeria.json, data/csv/wilayas.csv, data/sql/full.sql,
   data/geojson/wilayas.geojson and algeria.geojson.

   The other 63 wilaya capital points are the centres of communes with no
   recorded source, are not OpenStreetMap-derived and no ODbL claim is made over
   them.

